## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses capability to design scalable, tenant-aware CAPA for a shared data platform, balancing fairness and speed while ensuring traceability.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and backpressure control
- Evidence collection and artifact management
- Lifecycle state machine design
- REST API design for CAPA with logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics and RCA structuring
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

